in paris protesters and police have  clashed during a march against france's  so-called health pass  the pass requires proof of vaccination  against covet 19  or a negative test to enter many public  venues  and lawmakers are now debating making it  even stricter  in the hope that it'll persuade more  people to get the jab  but the demonstrators say the measures  breached their civil liberties  shrouded in clouds of tear gas the city  of light dissolved  into a battleground as police and  protesters clashed  over proposed covet 19 restrictions  rallies were held across paris on  saturday against a bill being debated by  lawmakers which passed its first reading  the day before  the new measures would require everyone  in france  to have a special virus pass to go to  restaurants and other venues  it would also make vaccinations  compulsory for healthcare workers  i'm absolutely against it because i'm  not vaccinated  on september the 15th if i'm not  vaccinated i will lose my job  i have been threatened with the sack i'm  here today in favor of the freedom to  choose to get vaccinated or not  we need to wait a little bit before the  french people can decide  i feel that we are being rushed it's  only been six months since these  vaccines were made widely available  and it feels like french people are  being forced i think a part of france is  always going to be unwilling  kovic 19 infections are spiking once  more across france  and hospital admissions are also on the  increase  the government has responded by speeding  up its vaccination campaign  to protect the most vulnerable and also  avoid  fresh lockdowns despite the threat of  water cannon  these protesters at least refused to  back down  against the proposal for a nationwide  coronavirus pass
 

